# Project conventions

Living rule for this repo. Add new sections here as conventions settle — do not create one-off rules for every topic unless the concern needs its own file/globs (e.g. Postman).

Canonical style/layout law: `docs/style.md` + `docs/architecture.md`. Agent checklist that must always apply: [`.cursor/rules/go-style.mdc`](go-style.mdc). This file points at docs and captures process that is not code style.

## Docs map

| Path | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `docs/architecture.md` | Layout, env flags, auth, health |
| `docs/style.md` | Lint, module file layout, HTTP patterns |
| `docs/adr/` | Accepted architecture decisions (why we chose X) |
| `docs/backlog.md` | Deferred gaps / tech debt — come back later |
| `docs/eventing/` | Topics, schemas, runbook |
| `docs/README.md` | Index of the above |

## Backlog (`docs/backlog.md`)

### Purpose

Park known gaps, tech debt, and deferred design work discovered while building. Not a product roadmap. Not an ADR — ADRs record **decided** architecture; backlog records **open** follow-ups.

### When to add an item

- Something works for now but has a clear hole (e.g. orphan files after two-step upload)
- You choose not to fix it in the current change
- Future-you (or an agent) should find it without hunting chat history

### How to write an item

Append under the `---` in `docs/backlog.md`:

```markdown
## Short title

- Area: module / platform (e.g. `file` + `post`)
- Status: open | parked | done
- Context: 1–3 lines — what happens today
- Next: concrete follow-up when we return
```

Keep entries short. Link related code paths or docs if helpful.

### How to close an item

- Fixed in code → delete the section (or mark `done` then remove in the same PR)
- Became a lasting decision → move the substance into a new `docs/adr/NNNN-….md` and remove from backlog

### Agent behavior

- When the user parks a follow-up (“we'll come back to this”), **add or update** an entry in `docs/backlog.md` in the same session unless they say not to
- Before inventing a new cleanup/GC feature that might already be listed, **read** `docs/backlog.md`
- Do not treat backlog items as committed work unless the user asks to implement one

## Extending this rule

Add new `##` sections below for project-wide conventions (seed flow, env/secrets, module scaffolding, deploy notes, …). Prefer one always-on file over many tiny always-on rules. Use a separate `.mdc` with `globs` only when the rule is file-type specific.

## Postman

When creating or editing anything under `postman/`, **read and follow** [`.cursor/rules/postman-collections.mdc`](postman-collections.mdc) (naming, `base_url`/`root_url`, snake_case vars, dynamic payload vars). Do not invent a parallel style.
